    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0716" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Marshall to General Hsu
                            Yung-chang</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">OSE 36</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-15">May 15, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The enclosed memorandum from General Chou En-lai<anchor n="28" xml:id="d328-f1"/>
                    concerning the Canton Communists is forwarded for your information. This
                    memorandum shows that General Chou En-lai has approved the amount of 374,086,000
                    CNC which is to be set aside for handling the expenses incident to the
                    evacuation of the Communists from that area. The memorandum further indicates
                    that the Communist Party will probably be able to furnish any additional sums
                    which might be required.</p>
                <p>I would like to point out that there are at present three U. S. Navy LST’s at
                    Canton for the purpose of evacuating the Communists, but that these LST’s must
                    be released by 20 May. It is apparent from this that the shipping now available
                    cannot be used to evacuate the Communists unless evacuation commences prior to
                    20 May. However, it is requested that you inform General Chang Fa Kwei of
                    General Chou’s approval in order that all arrangements can be facilitated in the
                    hope <pb facs="0717" n="705" xml:id="pg705"/> that in the near future other
                    shipping can be made available when the Communists assemble at the port of
                    embarkation.</p>
                <p>Executive Headquarters has been informed of General Chou’s approval and it too is
                    expediting action.</p>
                <closer>For <signed>General Marshall: <lb/> J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hart
                            Caughey</hi>
                    </signed><lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel, G. S. C.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
